Package: LaTerra
Title: La Terra: A Matrix-First Framework for Branch-Wise Comparative Genomics
Version: 0.0.0.9022
Authors@R: 
    person("Jiaqi", "Wu", email = "wujiaqi@hiroshima-u.ac.jp", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A matrix-first framework and evolving R-native platform for
    auditable branch-wise comparative genomics on supplied coordinate-valid
    matrices. Provides explicit binary-trait input readers, recipe inspection,
    a historical S2 computation route, saved-result diagnostics, bounded reports,
    and plots without refitting. Marine/S2 is the first exact-replay historical
    example, not a restriction on the framework's future scope. Provides
    lightweight S3 objects, configuration containers, and provenance contracts.
    Implements the trait-independent nonnegative C3
    margin-working-mean baseline with explicit graph, boundary, facial-set,
    deterministic fitting, and certificate contracts. Adds trait-free,
    threshold-free descriptive geometry diagnostics for materialized rate
    representations without changing scientific inputs or eligibility. The
    current log-relative contract is boundary aware: positive GBI values have
    finite natural-log coordinates, exact observed zeros with positive
    denominator are mathematical boundaries, and unavailable causes remain a
    separate compact ledger. ZERO_MASS and POSITIVE_LOG are separate
    association and calibration components with no joint p-value. Historical
    finite-sentinel logGBI objects are read/migrate-only; their global-k10 view
    is diagnostic/replay-only, is refused by ordinary inference, and can be
    checked against separately supplied source and replay authorities. Adds
    exact-keyed branch-state objects, Layer-5 association domains, unweighted
    point estimands, and empirical calibration against externally supplied
    coherent branch-state null worlds without generating or adjudicating a
    scientific null.
